cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you utilize this empirical dataset, econometric codebase, or methodology in academic research, policy analysis, or valuation benchmarks, please cite it as below."
title: "NJUDS Computational Spatial Econometrics & Multi-Modal Underwriting Benchmark"
authors:
  - family-names: Gonzalez
    given-names: Dorian Mario
    email: dorianmariogonzalez@gmail.com
    affiliation: "New Jersey Underwriting Data Systems (NJUDS) — Computational Econometrics Research Lab"
abstract: >
  An open-science computational spatial econometrics framework and multi-modal valuation
  benchmark designed for legacy urban housing stock. Resolves hedonic Automated Valuation Model
  (AVM) pricing failures in pre-1940 structures by integrating high-throughput Scatter-Gather
  computer vision pipelines (eliminating the Vision Token Tax), statutory New Jersey Chapter 123
  (N.J.S.A. 54:51A-6) assessment equalization corridor modeling, Uniform Construction Code (NJ UCC)
  permitting friction, and multi-layer GIS environmental hazard intersections.
version: 1.0.0
